<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.10.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02261</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.10.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0b1a5851-9874-46bb-ad75-7ef0ecfc1ac3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="5f65cc8d-fbf0-4264-985d-80ccbb2ee4f4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 1 – 4, find the factored form of the quadratic expression.</para><para>\(3x^2+ 16x + 5\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((3x − 5)(x − 1)\)</para><para>\((3x + 1)(x - 5)\)</para><para>\((3x − 1)(x − 5)\)</para><para>\((3x + 1)(x + 5)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \((3x + 1)(x + 5)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="885451ea-6a0d-43bb-a2e2-66dcec6ebf4d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(2x^2+ 11x − 6\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2x + 6)(x − 1)\)</para><para>\((2x − 6)(x + 1)\)</para><para>\((2x − 1)(x + 6)\)</para><para>\((2x + 1)(x − 6)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \((2x − 1)(x + 6)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="71fed853-ac3a-4c2b-acca-01fd838d8b32" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2− 13x + 3\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4x − 1)(x − 3)\)</para><para>\((4x + 3)(x + 1)\)</para><para>\((4x − 3)(x − 1)\)</para><para>\((4x + 1)(x + 3)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \((4x − 1)(x − 3)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="7bd97612-9bcd-4e35-b7a2-71ad543b985b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(2x^2−3x −2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2x + 1)(x − 2)\)</para><para>\((2x + 2)(x − 1)\)</para><para>\((2x − 2)(x + 1)\)</para><para>\((2x − 1)(x + 2)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \((2x + 1)(x − 2)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="0a46316d-2d16-4e78-a061-e7272eae6ee9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The height, in meters, of a baseball being hit is modeled by the function \(h(x) = -2x^2+ 12x + 3\) where \(x\) is the number of seconds since being hit.
          
          Approximately how many seconds pass before the baseball lands on the ground? Use graphing technology if needed.
        </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>4.38 seconds</para><para>6.24 seconds</para><para>7.26 seconds</para><para>7.56 seconds</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is 6.24 seconds .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="06fd0036-d5b6-4199-96e0-4ecf8c671b62" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The height, in meters, of a roller coaster is modeled by the function \(h(x) = -2x^2 + 20x + 5\) where \(x\) is the number of seconds after starting.
          
          Approximately how many seconds pass before the roller coaster reaches the ground? Use graphing technology if needed.
        </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>5.221 seconds</para><para>7.963 seconds</para><para>8.365 seconds</para><para>10.244 seconds</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.10.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 10.244 seconds .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="b796bb7a-1f2a-422c-995b-d498e03b9a34" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 7 – 10, find the factored form of the quadratic expression.</para><para>\(3x^2 + 2x − 5\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((3x + 5)(x + 1)\)</para><para>\((x + 5)(3x − 1)\)</para><para>\((3x + 5)(x − 1)\)</para><para>\((3x − 5)(x + 1)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para><para>The correct answer is \((3x + 5)(x − 1)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c7c95a68-b05d-4b64-84d7-e872ef7f7687" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4x^2+ 4x − 15\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4x − 3)(x + 5)\)</para><para>\((2x − 3)(2x + 5)\)</para><para>\((4x + 3)(x − 5)\)</para><para>\((2x + 3)(2x − 5)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para><para>The correct answer is \((2x − 3)(2x + 5)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="9523d2c9-fddb-4b93-bb3e-1e5f0ad6a8df" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(5x^2− 39x − 8\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((5x − 1)(x + 8)\)</para><para>\((5x + 8)(x − 1)\)</para><para>\((5x − 8)(x + 1)\)</para><para>\((5x + 1)(x − 8)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5. </para><para>The correct answer is \((5x + 1)(x − 8)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d36f22e4-b400-4555-8a81-111a108f6e0b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(6x^2+ 53x − 9\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((6x − 1)(x + 9)\)</para><para>\((3x − 1)(2x + 9)\)</para><para>\((2x − 1)(3x + 9)\)</para><para>\((6x + 1)(x − 9)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.10.2 and 8.10.5.</para><para>The correct answer is \((6x − 1)(x + 9)\) .
      </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
